Cleaning Technique No. 1: Decide What Goes Where!

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:57.250
This place gets messy because

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:57.250
things are just left scattered all over the floor. 

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:01.410
That's why we have to decide

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:01.410
where each and every item goes. 

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:01.540
REMOTE

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:01.540
CONTROLS

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.500
I'd like you to use the bookshelves. 

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:05.200
Roger that!

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:12.160
I wonder where Big Brother learned his technique...

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:15.790
Detox of the Heart

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:15.790
It's Cleaned Up All of America.

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:15.750
From THIS, huh?

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:22.160
We've pretty much figured out where things go, huh?

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:24.290
But there's a whole bunch still left over. 

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:29.040
Cleaning Technique

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:29.040
Number 2

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:29.040
"Store Whatever Remains Left from Step 1"

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:28.870
Cleaning Technique No. 2:

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:28.870
Store Whatever Remains Left from Step 1!

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:32.950
If you can't come up with a place for something,

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:32.950
it means you don't use it much and you should store it. 

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:31.040
Stream

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:31.040
Rider

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:36.410
Let's box up volumes

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:36.410
of the same size and genre together. 

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:43.660
But Big Brother, what "genre" is it

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:43.660
if you've got a DVD inside of a game case?

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:45.870
Why do you have things all mixed up like that?

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:50.290
It's a pain to keep pulling discs out and

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:50.290
putting them back in, so I just put them wherever...

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:52.330
Put them back in their proper cases!

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:57.290
Okay, that's everything nice and stored. 

00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:00.620
But if there's no more room to put stuff?

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:02.660
Presenting Cleaning Technique No. 3:

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:03.830
Cleaning Technique

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:03.830
Number 3

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:03.830
"Toss It!"

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:04.040
You toss it!

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:10.620
JIBA DOG

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:08.750
HUH?! No way! That would be a waste!

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:08.750
I mean, look how cute this doll thing is!

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:10.250
You call that "cute"?

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:14.540
Listen closely, Umaru:

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:14.540
All things are destined to meet their end!

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:18.370
Out with the old and in with the new!

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:18.370
This is the natural order of things!

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.790
Out with the old and in with the new!

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.790
This is the natural order of things!

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.790
Hup, hup!

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:22.580
THIS!

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:24.790
Detox

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:24.790
of the Heart

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:24.120
That includes this, right?

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:29.700
The sticky note on this page here

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:29.700
says the same thing that you're saying.  

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:36.620
M-maybe I could keep that

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:36.620
stuffed doll of yours on my desk... 

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:38.370
You don't mind?!

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:42.250
Looks pretty clean, doesn't it?

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:43.830
Yeah!

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:46.160
Flying leap!

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:51.040
All that's left is to see

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:51.040
if you can keep things nice and neat.  

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:53.290
The Next Day

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:58.000
I'm bored of this game... oh, I know!

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:01.040
I'll play one of those retro games

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:01.040
that turned up yesterday.

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:04.370
I AM

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:04.370
JUJOMARU!

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.750
It's fun to play these once in a while. 

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:14.290
Why do you have things all mixed up like that?

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:17.330
Which case did this belong to...?

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:20.540
The Following Sunday

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:34.330
Umaru... You can leave things a LITTLE messy... 

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:38.950
He's all shriveled up. 

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:48.450
Are you going somewhere on Sunday?

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:51.120
We're going to the movies!

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:57.700
This is a big crowd indeed!

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:04.160
It's been a while since I've seen a movie at the theater.

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:05.950
What do you think? Should we watch it first, or...?

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:08.910
Well, it is almost lunch time. 

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:09.750
Yeah, that's true. 

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:18.410
Sylphyn has already bought popcorn

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:18.410
